      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:6:2:3",
      "text": [
        " إِنَّ رَسُولَ اللَّهِ ( صلى الله عليه وآله ) قَالَ كُلُّ ذِي نَابٍ مِنَ السِّبَاعِ وَ مِخْلَبٍ مِنَ الطَّيْرِ حَرَامٌ وَ قَالَ ( عليه السلام ) لَا تَأْكُلْ مِنَ السِّبَاعِ شَيْئاً."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Hammad, from Al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘Rasool-Allah<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘All the ones with fangs from the predatory animals, and claws from the birds, are Prohibited’. And he<sup>saww</sup> said: ‘Do not eat anything from the predators’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "3. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘ Umayr from Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said that the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, grant compensation to Muhammad and his family worthy of their services to Your cause, has said, ‘Of the beasts that which have canine teeth and of birds that which have claws are not lawful for food.’ He (the Imam) has said, ‘Do not use any of the beasts for food.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
